    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the level rules with a points system per the specification.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Reworked the derived membership logic:\n- Added `getMembershipPoints()` (`@Transient`): starts at 0, `+2` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+ (`householdMemberCount >= 3`), `+3` for tenure over 365 days.\n- `getMembershipLevel()` now maps points \u2192 level: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+), instead of the old direct-factor computation.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `membershipPoints` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it), and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the new mapping.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with an email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
