    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:133`), taking an `OwnerFieldsDto` and persisting an `Owner` entity.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **Authorization gate** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:131`). Non-admins get 403 before the method runs.\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 triggered by `@Valid`/`@Validated` on the generated `OwnersApi` interface (`OwnersApi.java:86`, `:44`). Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern((?s).*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (nullable)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`, `@Email` (nullable)\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (nested, no real effect)\n   - *(No custom `ConstraintValidator`s exist.)*\n\n3. **Manual field normalization + validation** \u2014 `normalizeAndValidateFields(owner)` (`:135-137`, `:177-202`), each returning 400 on failure:\n   - **Address**: trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded; empty \u2192 400.\n   - **Email** (if present): trimmed/lower-cased; must match `EMAIL_PATTERN`; rejected if a disposable domain (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com).\n   - **Postcode**: must be valid 4-digit code within the region range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099).\n   - **Telephone**: normalized to E.164 (`+61`, drop leading 0); must match `E164_PATTERN` with valid national-number length.\n\n4. **Future registration date** \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 400 (`:138-141`).\n\n5. **Per-day create limit** \u2014 \u2265 100 owners already registered on that date \u2192 429 (`:144-146`).\n\n6. **Duplicate identity check** \u2014 matching `identityKey` (telephone|email|household) against all existing owners \u2192 409 (`:149-151`).\n\n7. **Household-sharing check** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` is false but a housemate already exists in the same household \u2192 409 (`:152-155`).\n\n8. **City-capacity check** \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in that city \u2192 409 (`:156-158`).\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\n9. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` creates the `Owner` (`:134`).\n\n10. **Field overwrites from normalization** \u2014 address, email, and telephone fields are mutated to their normalized values (during step 3 above).\n\n11. **Registration date resolved/set** \u2014 uses supplied date or `LocalDate.now()`, then rolled forward off weekends to a business day; written back via `setRegistrationDate` (`:142-143`).\n\n12. **householdId + identityKey set** \u2014 SHA-256-derived values (`:147-148`).\n\n13. **Derived registration attributes assigned** \u2014 `assignRegistrationAttributes(...)` (`:159`) sets: `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId` (again), `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount`, and `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` flags.\n\n14. **Database INSERT** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 `em.persist` inside a `@Transactional` boundary; assigns the generated id (`:160`).\n\n15. **Audit log line** \u2014 dedicated `AUDIT` logger emits one INFO line on success (`:161-162`).\n\n16. **Location header** \u2014 `Location: /api/owners/{id}` set on the response (`:163-165`).\n\n17. **Response DTO with derived `bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 `buildOwnerDto(owner)` maps to `OwnerDto` and sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners registered today); returns 201 (`:166`).\n\n## Notably absent on this path\nNo password encoding, no event publishing, no emails/notifications, no cache updates, and no JPA auditing/`@PrePersist`. Importantly, the **`Owner` entity's own Bean Validation annotations are never re-triggered** \u2014 the hand-written `EntityManager.persist` doesn't invoke a validator, so only the `OwnerFieldsDto` constraints (step 2) actually fire."
